# agent-lifecycle-seed

Synthetic fixture for three probes: `agent-lifecycle-seed-probe`, `agent-lifecycle-core-probe` and
`agent-own-evidence-probe`. They guard one defect: a sub-agent ends with a hand-back tail in its OWN transcript
(`agent-<id>.jsonl`), the parent transcript never records a completion for it, and the session list kept saying
`running` long after the agent was done.

Nothing here comes from a real session. Every record is built by hand in `build-fixture.js` from the SHAPE of a real
one (record types and keys); ids, text and paths are neutral. The timestamps are literal constants, chosen so the
literals hard-coded in the probes hold.

## Layout

Same relative layout as one project folder under `~/.claude/projects`. A probe places this directory (or a copy, or
symlinks to its files) as ONE project folder inside a throwaway projects root (`CLAUDE_DECK_PROJECTS_DIR=<root>`);
`findSessionFile` only descends one level, so the root must hold it.

    00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a001.jsonl                         main transcript, 7 records
    00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a001/subagents/
        agent-a0000000000000a01.jsonl                                  the sub-agent's own transcript, 22 records
        agent-a0000000000000a01.meta.json                              the dispatch meta (matched by toolUseId)
    build-fixture.js                                                   regenerates the three files

Neutral values: session id `00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000a001`, agent id `a0000000000000a01`, dispatch id (the
parent's `Agent` tool_use) `toolu_00000000000000000000d001`, cwd `/home/user/project`, version `0.0.0`.

## What the gates read

Main transcript (parent side):

| record | ts | role |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | 17:35:29.174Z | the `Agent` dispatch (`subagent_type`, `run_in_background`): the ledger entry keyed by the dispatch id |
| 2 | 17:35:54.370Z | the async-launch ack with `toolUseResult.agentId`: joins the dispatch to the own file |
| 3, 4 | 17:51:46.045Z | the parent-side "waiting" notice (queue-operation + queued_command), 6 ms after the first own tail |
| 5, 6 | 17:57:45Z, 17:58:30Z | the parent keeps writing after the final tail |

The main transcript holds NO completion for the dispatch id (no non-waiting task notification, no non-ack result for
it): a ledger `final` would win over the own tail and hide the defect.

Own transcript (all `isSidechain: true`, 0-based indices):

| index | ts | role |
|---|---|---|
| 5-7, 8-10 | 17:46-17:50 | two background children, each opened by an assistant `run_in_background` tool_use and closed by its task notification (`maxOpen` 1, back to 0) |
| 11, 12, 13 | 17:51:45.308Z .. 17:51:46.039Z | first tail: handback tool_use, its tool_result, the stop-hook attachment, 0 open children: the file is terminal here |
| 14 | 17:57:07.026Z | wake-up (a task notification as a user string): clears the terminal state, the agent runs again |
| 17, 18 | 17:57:11Z | end_turn answer, then a user string (not terminal: the stop is not last, no hand-back result yet) |
| 19, 20, 21 | 17:57:28.464Z .. 17:57:28.829Z | final tail: handback tool_use -> tool_result -> stop-hook attachment, all sidechain. The documented tail |
| 2 | none | an `api-request-blob` with no timestamp, so the fold's "no usable ts counts for nothing" path stays covered |

Terminal prefixes of the own file are exactly indices 13 and 21 (`seed_terminal_only_on_stop_tail`). The gap between the
first tail (17:51:46.039Z) and the wake-up (17:57:07.026Z) is the window where the parent's waiting notice must not
beat the own tail (`own_tail_wins_over_parent_waiting_notice`).

## Changing it

Edit `build-fixture.js`, run `node test/fixtures/agent-lifecycle-seed/build-fixture.js`, then update, in the probes,
the byte sizes pinned by `fixture_intact` (agent-lifecycle-seed-probe), the record count of `seed_fixture_present` and
the terminal indices of `seed_terminal_only_on_stop_tail` (agent-lifecycle-core-probe). Keep the timestamps the probes
hard-code: 17:51:46.039Z (first tail), 17:57:07.026Z (wake-up), 17:57:28.829Z (final tail).

To see the gates guard the defect, drop the last three records of the own transcript (the final tail) and run the seed
and own-evidence probes: the tail gates fail.
